cluding ignored editor_assets/node_modules binaries such as the Mach-O esbuild executable. tests/unit/test_attestation_signing.py::test_hook_falls_back_to_git_when_env_unset clones the current checkout and fails when it is a shallow promisor clone with unavailable historical objects. These are test-hygiene defects, not runtime failures.\n\n## Plan\n- Make the shipped-surface test enumerate tracked/package-shipped textual inputs rather than arbitrary working-tree artifacts.\n- Make the build-provenance test construct a self-contained minimal Git fixture or explicitly materialize/guard required objects.\n- Add negative controls for an ignored binary under the source tree and for a shallow/partial source checkout.\n- Keep both tests behavioral: stale shipped command tokens and Git-fallback build provenance must still fail when broken.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The shipped-surface contract passes with an ignored non-UTF-8 binary under src/rebar and still fails when the retired token appears in a shipped text file.\n- [ ] The provenance fallback test does not depend on the audit checkout having a complete object database.\n- [ ] The provenance test still proves the wheel embeds git rev-parse --short HEAD when REBAR_BUILD_COMMIT is unset.\n- [ ] Targeted tests pass in full and shallow/promisor checkout fixtures.\n- [ ] No broad decode-error swallowing or unconditional skip weakens either oracle.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","reason":"Scope the source scan to shipped textual inputs and add a binary negative control."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_attestation_signing.py","reason":"Use a self-contained Git fixture and cover partial-checkout behavior."},{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"Only if a reusable partial-checkout fixture belongs at suite scope."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d33918c5-e2b5-472b-89af-75c8ec737c3c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["testing","test-hygiene","git","audit-follow-up"],"ticket_id":"def1-9c3c-6802-48bd","ticket_type":"task","title":"Harden source-scan and local-clone tests for generated artifacts and partial checkouts","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["32bf10d9-c163-4762-8a31-b44dea0b19c1","26b5420b-49a6-4ddc-9222-4d7fee17d64b","8ba7bbb7-2aac-45b2-a044-dcbdc0ef9c43","21755c17-589f-45d7-87e2-8efbb05056fa","d33918c5-e2b5-472b-89af-75c8ec737c3c","8c93ad55-31a6-429a-b070-df55a7e2deca"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786501904810345002,"uuid":"f5599340-9550-4c7e-87c1-14c4e03d98a0"}